{"t": 43.091, "n": 47, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "No spec states G4 as package-level behaviour. The closest precedent is the independent review unit, and it's the model to follow. I'm reporting from reads only and have not confirmed any claim against code or tests.\n\nARTIFACT gap_finding: No spec states G4 at package level; searched `plugins/temperspec-tgraph/docs/specs` and `plugins/tempergraph/docs/specs` for \"back_target\", \"trip back\" and \"findings\", and read `code-mode.spec.md`, `code-join.spec.md`, `phase-coding.spec.md` and `budgets-and-failures.spec.md`. The closest model is `independent-review.spec.md`, which sends numbered findings back once. IRV-B9 and B10 pick the code or plan step, IRV-B11 gives the target the numbered blocking findings as its reason, IRV-B12 allows one trip back, and IRV-B13 pauses on a blocking finding left after the trip. `review-findings.spec.md` RVF-B2 to B5 define the numbered item form (number, file:line, mark, text). The engine's `budgets-and-failures.spec.md` has BUD-B3 (a back-edge unit's budget counts per visit) and BUD-B4 (a trip back clears the verdicts of the target and later units), with nothing on a budget of one trip or an environment failure pausing at once. `code-mode.spec.md` CDM-B7 (lines 53-57) runs expand, phase items, then code on `phases`, with no return to the join; its open question (line 110) keeps the first arm after a trip back. `phase-coding.spec.md` PHC-B14 and B15 (lines 115-124) cover only a trip back to the plan step. `code-join.spec.md` (lines 1-12) is a route with no session, check or effect, and has no back target.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "1c380d38-33ab-43bd-bd0a-85f831bcc092"}
